Hi,

I have come across a problem using DEC's X25 layered product on 
DIGITAL UNIX 3.0 running on an alpha based DEC 3000 model 600s

The call X25OpenPVC fails to return while linking with the threaded 
version of the library. When the same code is linked with the 
normal (un-threaded) version the code works fine.
Is this a known problem ? Any help would be most welcome.
regards
Rajiv

Note : Below is a extract from the program which is currently working 
under normal process environment and not working in the threaded environment.

/*****************
*/
#define MAIN
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <netx25/x25.h>
#include <errno.h>
#include <setjmp.h>
#include <pthread.h>

main()
{
    int result,cid;

    if((result = X25OpenPort()) < 0)
    {
        char errorText[50];
        strcpy(errorText, "** Could not open port");
        X25PrintError(result, errorText);
        exit(0);
    }

    cid = result;

    if((result = X25OpenPVC(cid,0,NULL,0,"simpact-pvc")) < 0)
    {
        char errorText[50];
        strcpy(errorText, "** Could not open PVC");
        X25PrintError(result, errorText);
        exit(0);
    }

    while(1)
    {
      sleep(1);
    }
  
}




