wilkinan wrote:
> On Solaris (for example), I can create a shared object, and then
> from an application (which hasn't been compile-time linked with
> that shared object), do something like:
> handle = dlopen("mylib.so");
> pfunc  = dlsym(handle);
> 
> i = (*pfunc)();
> 
> dlclose(handle);
> 
> Is there a similar mechanism on DEC UNIX (OSF/1)? Or is there
> any software around capable of achieving the same end as this.

Digital Unix supports the dlopen(), dlclose(), and dlsym() funcitons. 
These are supported in Digital Unix V3.2. 
I am not sure which prior releases did support those functions. There
are some differences between the Sun and Digital implementations. In the
future, there will be a standard version of these accross platforms.

