x-mailer: Mozilla 2.0b6 (X11; I; OSF1 V3.0 alpha)

Casey Kolehmainen wrote:
> 
> Does anyone know the process of adding a non-DEC disk to an Alpha/OSF system?

Well, the only real difference is that the DEC drives already have an entry
in /etc/disktab - for a non-DEC drive you'll have to write one yourself
using /sbin/scu (or the drive documentation) to get the numbers.  It's
fairly tolerant - as long as your numbers come out pretty close to the total
number of logical blocks it won't quibble over the number of sectors per
track or whatever.  This is a good thing 'cause those numbers are dynamic
anyway.

Instructions for adding a second drive are summarized at
http://csugrad.cs.vt.edu/handbook/newdisk-osf.html.  That page is aimed at
Virginia Tech CS majors owning DEC 3000/300LX machines but most of it should
be correct.  One mistake I know of is the part where it tells you that you
have to recompile the kernel in order to add a second swap partition - I
think the author momentarily mixed up Ultrix and OSF/1 there.

