In article <4duvll$h5@noc.tor.hookup.net>, andyl@netinc.ca (Andy Leitzinger) writes:

>Hi,
>	I've got an Alpha server which does not have the help system 
>installed. I have the DEC UNIX v3.2 CD. Where do I find and how do I install 
>the help subsystem?

1.  Put CD in CD reader.
2.  Mount the CD at some convient mount point

	# mount -r /dev/rz#c /mnt

    Fill in the rz#c with the appropriate block device.

3.  Use the setld command to install the desired subsets:

	# setld -l /mnt/ALPHA/BASE

This will offer a menu of all the subsets not installed.  The
man (apropos and what) command are in the Document Preparation
subset (DCMT).  The manual pages split across a number of
subsets.  On V3.2A they are:

OSFMANOP320  - Programming
OSFMANWOP320 - Windows Programming
OSFMANOS320  - Admin/User
OSFMANWOS320 - Window Admin/User
OSFMANRT320  - Realtime

