references: <199601230647.AAA25153@pirates.cs.swt.edu> <4e3lrp$r7s@nntpd2.cxo.dec.com> <4e5m01$9hd@amhux3.amherst.edu>
organization: Virginia Tech, Blacksburg, Virginia
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,news.software.nntp

PAUL D. CHAPIN (pdchapin@unix.amherst.edu) wrote:

: So how do you set up the number of extents on the original volume?  I
: can see how to use the -x option with addvol, but the man page for
: mkfdmn doesn't mention and equivalent option.

You have to create the domain and then use mkfdmn/addvol sequence:  

# mkfdmn -x 1024 /dev/rz1g test_dmn
# addvol -x 1024 /dev/rz4g test_dmn

Yeah, it's not documented. Look in the release notes for the advfs
utilities. There's a short decription there. To find out the current
size of your extents area, do:

 cd whatever-fileset-you-want
 cd .tags
 showfile -x M-6

Look at the PageCnt column, ignore the first row and see if the others
sasy 1024. If they do, you ok, if not, you'll have to do the 
mkfdmn/addvol sequence above. m-6 is for a 1st volume Metadata table,
M-12 is a second volume Metadata table. (thanks to Rick Jackson for
this tidibit). 

