In article <4djfc1$h3q@news.ccit.arizona.edu> pardede@PROBLEM_WITH_YOUR_MAIL_GATEWAY_FILE (Ferdinand M. Pardede) wrote:

> Hi all,
> 

<Snip>

> In short, what should I do to get the root access again?  I tried to go to
> the single-user mode (by crashing the system), but it's quite primitive so
> I was afraid to do much in this mode.

a) Bring down the system as gracefully as possible under the circumstances.
b) Boot in single user mode. (B -FL S)
c) Do a bcheckrc. bcheckrc should mount your file systems for r/w.
d) Change the password for root using passwd.
e) sync (x3)
f) reboot

