|> alpha crashes??? i have osf1 v 3.2 
|> thanx
|> please do email me...
|> 				Federico
|> 


I sent some email off, but in case anyone runs into similar problems, 
the following might be useful...

If the system is crashing, dbx is just exposing a problem in the kernel
and is not directly responsible.  The only thing I know of in V3.2
was a problem with the vm space, which had a workaround.  It was usually seen
when quitting out of dbx, so I don't know if its the same one, but
the solution for that was the following:


Add these two lines to /etc/sysconfigtab (which is normally just a header file)


vm:
       vm-segmentation = 0x0

and then reboot the system.  This helped a number of customers, so it
might be worth a try.  An upgrade to V3.2c will also likely resolve the
problem. Let me know if this does not help.

PeterT



