Sorry, the correct usage is:
	/usr/sbin/disklabel -w -r /dev/rrz14a /dev/rrz14a
or
	/usr/sbin/disklabel -wn -r /dev/rrz14a /dev/rrz14a, if you don't
	want the bootstrap code on disk

And check if you have valid device entries for your disk:
	/usr/bin/file /dev/rrz14a

If the correct disktype is reported, you should get a label that you
can edit with
	/usr/sbin/disklabel -e /dev/rrz14a

Good luck again,
Steffen.

