You must also make sure that the support for ISO9660 is built into the kernel.
By default, it is not.  If the above mount command doesn't work, run doconfig to
build a new kernel.  Make sure you select the 9660 option during this process
and reboot using the newly made kernel.

That should do it.

Dave



