Giorgio Lupieri wrote:
> 
> How can i use a CD-ROM as a dos file system in order to centralize
> cd-rom view, whith OSF1 o.s. on an ALFA 1000 dec?
Think, you wanna mount a CD-ROM (which contain a "DOS fs"). Right?
Most of DOS-CD's are formated with the iso9660 fs. So the mount
command must contain the right type for fs. It's under DEC Unix
"mount -t cdfs -o noversion /dev/rz4c /mnt"
Check with uerf, where your CD ROM is located and enter the
right /dev/ entry. It's now possible to exported /mnt for NFS
or to create a pathworks share.
  
best regards
dirk

