(I am reposting this due to lack of response on the first try.)

Our alpha running DEC OSF/1 V3.2 is experiencing a problem with processes
not going away after the user terminates his session.  By terminate I mean
aborting a telnet session, which should normally send a hangup (SIGHUP) to
all processes connected to the users tty port.  The hangup signal never
gets sent, leaving numerous processes still running.  This was verified by
manually sending a hangup with "kill -HUP proc_ID", in which case the
process promptly dies.  As a partial solution we use a special killer
script which kills off all processes in the 'R' state with at least 2
minutes of CPU time, cycling every minute.  Even with this we have peak
periods during the day where the number of zombies will bring the system to
a crawl (or worse) and have to resort to manual zapping.  On our DEC ULTRIX
machine this problem does not occur, even though the exact same type of
session aborting occurs.

I checked the gettydefs file and all lines have the HUPCL flag as required.

Has anyone had a similar experience with hung processes, and if so, what did
you do to fix it?  Any comments/suggestions would be greatly appreciated.

