marek.pola@mailbox.swipnet.se (Marek Pola) wrote:

> Howdy, hackers.
> 
> On my company we are using NIS to distribute userids and passwords. I would 
> like to start using C2 as well, and have tried to implement it. It seems 
> however that while I can get the client to get all the userids from the NIS 
> server into the C2 database (/tcb/files/auth/[a-z]/*), it doesn't seem that a 
> change of password the user makes on a client is propagated back to the NIS 
> server.

The prpasswd map isn't exported/pushed by default. Edit the file /var/adm/Makefile
and change the action for "all:" to also build prpasswd (Defined later in the file).
The whole course of action is described in the Security Manual.

> 
> The functionality I would like is that the clients should have a high level of 
> security, including a need to change passwords at a specified interval, but 
> also that a user can one day sit down at another client machine, connected to 
> the same NIS server, and use the same userid and password. This works now when 
> we only are using NIS.

Do you mean that you want them to use the passwords in the passwd map (that aren't kept
in synch with those in prpasswd ) ?

You also might want to consider exporting the /tcb hiearchy using NFS instead of NIS.



