(1) If your version of Digital UNIX does not have pfopen.c in
/usr/examples, it's probably because the same module is now
in the standard C library.  This has been true for several
versions by now.

(2) Recent versions of Digital UNIX (and DEC OSF/1) have included
a precompiled version of nfswatch in one of the subsets, so there
should be no need to compile it yourself.

(3) Remember to rebuild your kernel to include the packet filter,
and to create the necessary entries in /dev.  See "man
packetfilter" for details.

-Jeff



