In my printcap are two entries:

lp1|1:\
        :af=/usr/adm/lp1acct:\
        :if=/usr/lbin/hplaser4psof:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lp1err:\
        :lp=:\
        :of=/usr/lbin/hplaser4psof:\
        :rm=inpon:\
        :rp=text:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd1:
lp|lp2|2|hp4m:\
        :af=/usr/adm/lp2acct:\
        :fc#0177777:\
        :fs#020:\
        :if=/usr/lbin/hplaser4psof:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lp2err:\
        :lp=:\
        :of=/usr/lbin/hplaser4psof:\
        :rm=inpon:\
        :rp=raw:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd2:\
        :sh:

The first is for postscript and the second is for text. There are problems
with full page graphics overflowing the HP , that seem to be related to
a problem with lpd on DU3.2 (214). Those problems may have been fixed 
in later versions (3.2c etc) but I have been trying to decide how to replace
lpd and what to replace it with. (My DU is running the Japanese LV). A binary
conversion of the Ultrix 4.4 lpd would work for non-Asian locales.

The real bottom line for what you are trying to do is that lpd completely
ignores outputfilters for remote printers. You need to handle it with a
script replacement or with an input filter. The "of" lines in my printcap
entries are ignored completely. It is a "feature"!

