You cannot expect a gettydefs banner in front of tcp/ip based login
sessions, since they are not initiated by getty. You should see them,
however, for LAT and serial line connections. Unfortunately, the length
of the message to be displayed is rather restricted and this limit
is hardcoded into getty (as far as I remember).

BTW You should kill your getty processes after changing gettydefs - they
read the file only on startup.

Cheers
Steffen

