In this reply, I incorrectly stated that the kernel attributes for process
limits were in the generic subsystem. Rather, they are in the "proc" 
subsystem. So the line to add to /etc/sysconfigtab would be:

proc:
    max-proc-per-user=128

or you can use sysconfigdb(8)...

Sorry for the confusion

