We use aps-491.tgz, a package from linux which acts as a inputfilter for 
the printer. It works together with the pbmplus and gs package. For i.e. 
a deskjet 850C the filter starts a conversion chain i.e.:

file format 

   gif:   gif -> ppm -> pnm -> ps -> gs -> deskjet driver -> lp

In addition you need the file command from linux, which is more powerful 
than the genuine dUnix one (reads from the input stream).


