I've had no problem with the RFC1321 code running on Digital UNIX.  All
I did was modify global.h:

/* UINT4 defines a four byte word */
#if defined(__osf__) && defined(__alpha)
typedef unsigned int UINT4;
#else
typedef unsigned long int UINT4;
#endif

With this modification, the code works identically on ULTRIX, OpenVMS,
Digital UNIX, and Windows NT.

