>Yesterday I installed the wu-ftpd with an anonymous ftp
>account. Everything seems to work fine except, that I don't have any 
>syslog messages from the commands executed ( I have of course the log of
>the transferred files in the XFERLOG file) by an anon-user. A normal user
>works fine.

In your ftpaccess file, you should have this:

log commands anonymous,guest,real

If that doesn't help, try adding the -L option to ftpd in your
/etc/inetd.conf file. The ftpaccess file options should override command
line options however, so this shouldn't be necessary. You never know with
wu-ftpd though...

If that doesn't help, perhaps your /etc/syslogd.conf file isn't set up
properly.
