In the meantime I found a solution for my problem.  I just compiled the
syslog.c file in the support-directory of wu-ftpd and added it to the
libsupport.a. This did it. It seems that the syslog of libc is different
from the one with wu-ftpd

Here is the diff to WU-FTPD/support/makefiles/Makefile.osf
*** Makefile.osf.old	Thu Jan 04 19:04:51 1996
--- Makefile.osf	Thu Jan 04 18:52:51 1996
***************
*** 6,13 ****
  LFLAGS = 
  CFLAGS = -O -DDEBUG ${IFLAGS} ${LFLAGS}
  
! SRCS   = getusershell.c fnmatch.c strcasestr.c strerror.c strsep.c authuser.c
! OBJS   = getusershell.o fnmatch.o strcasestr.o strerror.o strsep.o authuser.o
  
  all: $(OBJS)
  	-rm -f libsupport.a
--- 6,13 ----
  LFLAGS = 
  CFLAGS = -O -DDEBUG ${IFLAGS} ${LFLAGS}
  
! SRCS   = getusershell.c fnmatch.c strcasestr.c strerror.c strsep.c authuser.c syslog.c
! OBJS   = getusershell.o fnmatch.o strcasestr.o strerror.o strsep.o authuser.o syslog.o
  
  all: $(OBJS)
  	-rm -f libsupport.a
***************
*** 46,48 ****
--- 46,50 ----
  
  ftw.o: ftw.c
  	${CC} ${CFLAGS} -c ftw.c
+ syslog.o: syslog.c
+ 	${CC} ${CFLAGS} -c syslog.c

