I received a solution via mail, for all those interested, here it is:

> This being the case, the user will
> want to grab this patch kit from the CSC: # OSF350-049.  This fixes
> several problems in ar related to compressed objects as well as similar
> bugs in nm, odump and libmld.a.
>
> With respect to the problem in general, there's two approaches (assuming
> they have the fixed ar):
>
> 1) the user can compile all the .o's with -compress and just ar them into
> an archive.  (ie: cc -c -compress *.c ; ar cr mylib.a *.o)
>
> 2) the user can compile all the .o's normally and use the 'Z' option to
> ar to compress them on the fly as they are added to the archive.  (ie:
> cc -c *.c ; ar crZ mylib.a *.o)
>
> Lastly, if the user doesn't want to take the patch kit, they can also use
> objZ directly on the .o's after using the old ar.  (ie: cc -c *.c ;
> ar crZ mylib.a *.o ; objZ *.o)
>
> Hope this helps.  I don't travel the news groups regularly, so please feel
> free to post this yourself.

