Kit-pui Wong (kpwong@harp.psy.cuhk.hk) wrote:
: I have installed the WorldWide Support (Chinese) on our 
: AlphaStation 200 4/166 for a while, it used to work fine. 
: A few weeks ago, DXterm refused to work and reported unresolvable
: symbols on the console window. DXterm is still "ln -s" to 
: "/usr/i18n/usr/bin/X11/dxterm". I have no idea how 
: to solve these errors after many trials.

You didn't mention what version of Digital UNIX you are using, but
it sounds like the dxterm is not picking up the correct libDXterm.so.
I don't know how the WorldWide Support kit handles this (maybe by
defining LD_LIBRARY_PATH to point to the right place), but my guess
is that you'll find the right libDXterm.so in /usr/i18n/usr/shlib.
If you set LD_LIBRARY_PATH to /usr/i18n/usr/shlib it should work.

Alfred

