Martin Ibert (mib@bb-data.de) wrote:
: Never ever even think of backing up /proc. Honestly, you don't want

There is also a fairly obnoxious bug in 3.2c, where (according to a DEC
source) they mistakenly allocated the same virtual node id for /proc and for 
root-on-advfs.

If /proc is mounted, a 'vdump /' incorrectly descends into /proc, spitting out 
all kinds of 'invalid argument' errors, and causing vdump to return an exit
code of 1 (which causes problems if you have automated backups).

I've also seen similar problems when using tar and find on the root filesystem.

If you are running v3.2c and have root on advfs you'd be well advised
to not use /proc unless you absolutely have to.

tony
